{"id":58481,"ord":167,"n_segments":204,"prev":58480,"next":58482,"doc":{"id":"68359","title":"68359_Zutty Singleton oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Zutty Singleton","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68359/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359"},"chapter":"Zutty's stroke and friends","title":"The friendship with Nesuhi Ertegun from 1939","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Dance asks where the friendship began; Zutty says from Nick's in 1939, when they played the Press Club in Washington for Nesuhi, whose father was the Turkish Ambassador.","period":"1939","year_from":1939,"year_to":1939,"words":90,"start":[258,1],"end":[258,11],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359#s58481","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Washington, D.C.","focus":1,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"National Press Club","focus":1,"city":"Washington, D.C."},{"name":"Nick's","focus":0,"city":"New York"}],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Nesuhi Ertegun","qid":"Q710748","n":1},{"name":"Joe Marsala","qid":"Q1691519","n":1},{"name":"Max Kaminsky","qid":"Q1912807","n":1},{"name":"Benny Morton","qid":"Q352013","n":1},{"name":"Teddy Wilson","qid":"Q506052","n":1},{"name":"Adele Girard","qid":"Q185204","n":1},{"name":"Nicks","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"His father","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":4,"theme_name":"Playing with and around Miles Davis","community":22,"community_name":"Bandstand fights, knives and tempers","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":258,"b":1,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Well now, where did this, where did this friendship with Nesuhi begin?"},{"p":258,"b":2,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"Oh from way back."},{"p":258,"b":3,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"From Nicks. In '39."},{"p":258,"b":4,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yes. He always loved you I gather?"},{"p":258,"b":5,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Because we went to Washington to play at the Press Club, for Nesuhi. Now"},{"p":258,"b":6,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yes."},{"p":258,"b":7,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"With Teddy Wilson, Maxie Kaminsky, Benny Morton on trombone, Joe Murgsald and his wife on harp. Adele Girard?"},{"p":258,"b":8,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"(Wydelie Gerarde?)"},{"p":258,"b":9,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Yes, (Wydelie Gerarde?). And we played naturally to a packed house. See, it was really terrific."},{"p":258,"b":10,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"His father was Ambassador then."},{"p":258,"b":11,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Yes, his daddy was the Turkish Ambassador."}]}